# Line endings are LF in the working tree on EVERY platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks text files out as CRLF, and every test
# that compares a fixture's bytes to what the code produces fails on an
# invisible \r: three precomputed QR matrices and three theme files did, on the
# first Windows run that got far enough to compare anything. The code writes LF
# and the fixtures are recorded as LF, so the working tree should hold LF too.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recorded bytes, not text — never touched, never normalised.
*.pptx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.m4a binary
*.wav binary
*.woff2 binary
